<GuideLayout
  title="Why Vertical Integration Improves Activewear Manufacturing Reliability"
  type="MANUFACTURING GUIDE"
  description="How vertically integrated activewear manufacturing improves fabric control, sampling speed, production communication, quality consistency and reorder reliability."
>
  <p>Vertical integration means more of the production workflow is coordinated within one manufacturing system. For activewear buyers, this can reduce communication gaps between fabric sourcing, sampling, cutting, sewing, inspection and packing.</p>

  <h2>Reliability Benefits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Faster feedback between sample room and production line.</li>
    <li>Better control over fabric approval and color matching.</li>
    <li>More consistent sewing standards across repeat orders.</li>
    <li>Clearer accountability when quality issues appear.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Buyers Should Still Check</h2>
  <p>Vertical integration is helpful, but buyers should still verify actual capacity, quality control records, sample timelines, production photos and export experience.</p>

  <h2>Fitclo Perspective</h2>
  <p>Fitclo uses a coordinated manufacturing workflow to help brands move from idea to sample to bulk production with fewer handoff errors and more stable repeatability.</p>
</GuideLayout>
